ct that there was indeed a well attested medieval legend equating Xanten with Troy. The inherited local pronunciation is Santen /ˈsan.tən/, but it has now been widely displaced by the spelling pronunciation. Xanten is the only German locality in X- (though there are a few Bavarian ones, such as Gsellmühle, which are pronounced with initial /ks/)."]],"senses":[[37296,"xanten","name","Xanten (a town in Lower Rhine, North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany)",0]]},"anerzögt":{"inflections":[["anerzögt","anerziehen","formal,plural,rare,second-person,subjunctive,subjunctive-ii,subordinate-clause"]]},"anmaßet":{"inflections":[["anmaßet","anmaßen","plural,second-person,subjunctive,subjunctive-i,subordinate-clause"]]},"annams":{"inflections":[["annams","annam","genitive"]]},"ansagtest":{"inflections":[["ansagtest","ansagen","indicative,preterite,second-person,singular,subordinate-clause"]]},"ausreiseerlaubnissen":{"inflections":[["ausreiseerlaubnissen","ausreiseerlaubnis","dative,definite,plural"]]},"auszubrennen":{"inflections":[["auszubrennen","ausbrennen","infinitive,infinitive-zu"]]},"epa":{"inflections":[["epa","einmannpackung","alternative,abbreviation"]]},"fortspüle":{"inflections":[["fortspüle","fortspülen","first-person,indicative,present,singular,subordinate-clause"]]},"führerbunkers":{"inflections":[["führerbunkers","führerbunker","genitive"]]},"gatsches":{"inflections":[["gatsches","gatsch","genitive"]]},"hohltauben":{"inflections":[["hohltauben","hohltaube","plural"]]},"rudelbildungen":{"inflections":[["rudelbildungen","rudelbildung","plural"]]},"sechsundzwanzigfache":{"inflections":[["sechsundzwanzigfache","sechsundzwanzigfach","feminine,nominative,singular,strong,without-article"]]},"siebzigstes":{"inflections":[["siebzigstes","siebzigste","neuter,nominative,singular,strong,without-article"]]},"silberfuchses":{"inflections":[["silberfuchses","silberfuchs","genitive"]]},"steifend":{"inflections":[["steifend","steifen","participle,present"]]},"wahnsinnsdinger":{"inflecti